{# Shared content + popover styles for home-gwern A/B/C variants.
   Wrapper pages set --gw-max / --gw-mx-l / --gw-mx-r and label themselves. #}

<style>
  .gwern-body {
    max-width: var(--gw-max, 38em);
    margin: 2rem var(--gw-mx-r, auto) 6rem var(--gw-mx-l, auto);
    padding-inline: clamp(1rem, 4vw, 3rem);
  }

  .gwern-body h1 {
    font-family: var(--serif, "Source Serif 4", Georgia, serif);
    font-weight: 600;
    font-size: 2.2rem;
    line-height: 1.1;
    margin: 0 0 0.2rem;
  }
  .gwern-body .gwern-email {
    font-family: var(--mono, ui-monospace, monospace);
    font-size: 0.85rem;
    margin: 0 0 1.2rem;
    opacity: 0.7;
  }
  .gwern-body p { line-height: 1.55; margin: 0 0 1.1em; hanging-punctuation: first last; }
  .gwern-body h2 {
    font-family: var(--serif, "Source Serif 4", Georgia, serif);
    font-size: 1rem;
    font-weight: 600;
    font-variant: small-caps;
    letter-spacing: 0.06em;
    text-transform: lowercase;
    margin: 2.4rem 0 0.5rem;
    color: var(--ink, #2a2820);
  }

  .places-work {
    list-style: none;
    padding: 0;
    margin: 0;
  }
  .places-work li { margin-bottom: 1rem; }
  .place-name {
    display: block;
    font-weight: 500;
    line-height: 1.35;
  }
  .place-org {
    display: block;
    margin-top: 0.15rem;
    font-size: 0.82em;
    line-height: 1.35;
    opacity: 0.68;
  }
</style>

<article class="gwern-body" id="main">

  <h1>Lee Wilkers</h1>
  <p class="gwern-email"><a href="mailto:lee@leewilkers.com">lee@leewilkers.com</a></p>

  <h2>about</h2>
  <p>Hi, I&rsquo;m Lee. I&rsquo;m based in Atlanta<span class="sn-marker" tabindex="0"><span class="sidenote-tooltip">The &ldquo;global health capital&rdquo; of the world &ndash; I&rsquo;ve worked with most major institutions in the area. <em>AKA</em>: city in a forest, hollywood of the south, the A, Hotlanta.<br><em>AUTBKA</em>: Terminus, 1830s &ndash; southern endpoint of the Western &amp; Atlantic Railroad.</span></span>, by way of the DC area<span class="sn-marker" tabindex="0"><span class="sidenote-tooltip">The data center capital of the world. DC stands for data center now if you didn&rsquo;t know.</span></span> &ndash; closer to cattle than the Capitol.</p>
  <p>Most of my work has been in public health and global health ethics.</p>
  <p>I&rsquo;ve led studies, built research partnerships, and turned evidence into publications, tools, and program decisions.</p>

  <p><strong>Some things I&rsquo;ve worked on:</strong></p>
  <ul>
    <li>organizational learning inside disease-control campaigns</li>
    <li>measuring campaign effectiveness beyond &ldquo;coverage&rdquo;</li>
    <li>public engagement on contested technologies, including gene drives</li>
    <li>care systems for survivors of intimate partner violence</li>
    <li>ecology for spaceflight</li>
  </ul>

  <p>I studied ecology along the James River at Virginia Commonwealth University in Richmond, then earned an MPH at Emory&rsquo;s Rollins School of Public Health.</p>

  <h2>places i&rsquo;ve worked</h2>
  <ul class="places-work">
    <li><span class="place-name">Focus Area on Compassion &amp; Ethics (FACE)</span><span class="place-org">The Task Force for Global Health</span></li>
    <li><span class="place-name">Evans Research Group (Intimate Partner Violence)</span><span class="place-org">Rollins School of Public Health, Emory University</span></li>
    <li><span class="place-name">Human Engagement Learning Platform (HELP)</span><span class="place-org">Rollins School of Public Health, Emory University</span></li>
    <li><span class="place-name">Franklin Microbial Ecology Lab</span><span class="place-org">Virginia Commonwealth University, Richmond, VA</span></li>
  </ul>

</article>
